          Core
        </div> <img src="https://content.partnerpage." srcset="https://content.partnerpage. 1x,https://content.partnerpage. 1.5x,https://content.partnerpage. 2x,https://content.partnerpage. 3x,https://content.partnerpage. 4x" alt="Core" loading="lazy" data-test-tier-image="" class="h-8 w-8 object-contain"></div> <div class="flex h-20 w-[200px] max-w-full self-center text-center"><img alt="Wintactix" src="https://content.partnerpage." srcset="https://content.partnerpage. 1x,https://content.partnerpage. 1.5x,https://content.partnerpage. 2x,https://content.partnerpage. 3x,https://content.partnerpage. 4x" loading="lazy" data-test-partner-logo="" class="h-full w-full object-contain"></div> <div data-test-availability="" class="flex"><div class="flex items-center gap-x-1 overflow-hidden rounded-full px-[6px] py-px bg-surface-success-subtle-pressed"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" data-test-availability-icon-true="" width="16px" height="16px" class="text-text-success"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M10 18a8 8 0 100-16 8 8 0 000 16zm3.707-9.293a1 1 0 00-1.414-1.414L9 10.586 7.707 9.293a1 1 0 00-1.414 1.414l2 2a1 1 0 001.414 0l4-4z" clip-rule="evenodd"></path></svg> <div data-test-availability-text="" class="truncate text-text">
            Accepting new clients
          </div></div></div> <div class="flex flex-col gap-y-2"><h2 title="Wintactix" data-test-partner-name="" class="notranslate truncate text-text typography-h5">
          Wintactix
        </h2> <!----> <div data-test-partner-description="" class="line-clamp-4 h-[80px] text-text-subtle">
          We work with teams using Attio who have a clear direction for how they want their CRM to support the business, but need an experienced partner to turn that direction into a concrete system. Clients work with us to crystallize their thinking. We help them reason through how the system should work across teams, make the necessary trade-offs explicit, and decide what to standardize versus where flexibility is worth keeping. Our philosophy • We believe clients use Attio because they already trust the Attio brand. Our role starts after that decision, by helping you get the maximum out of the platform you’ve chosen. • We believe most teams already have direction. What you need is help crystallizing that direction and turning it into something concrete inside Attio. • We believe teams add more tools because they don’t realize what their existing tools can handle. A big part of our work is showing you what can live inside Attio and helping you to commit to that. • We believe the most valuable part of consulting is thinking with the client. That means working through your ideas together, pressure-testing them, and making trade-offs explicit. • We believe clients want confidence. Confidence that you're using Attio correctly, that your approach makes sense, and that your’re not painting yourselves into a corner without realizing it. What we typically help with • Turning a rough idea into a concrete Attio setup • Defining objects, relationships, properties, and lists • Reconciling how different teams view and use the same data • Designing schemas that can support real, day-to-day usage • Implementing larger, structured builds rather than lightweight configuration Who we’re a good fit for • Clients who want an experienced partner to work through the system with them and make clear, opinionated decisions on the setup • Teams using Attio who have an idea of where they want to go, but aren’t confident they’re setting it up in the best way • Teams who want trade-offs made explicit early, rather than discovering limitations later • Clients who want their approach sanity-checked and validated • Teams using PostHog: we’re often a strong fit by default, as our sister agency focuses exclusively on PostHog consulting (HogHelper.com) Who we’re not a good fit for • Email sequencing and outbound execution • Outreach copywriting or campaign management • Small, one-off configuration tasks • Teams without clear ownership or intent on what they want to build Next steps If this sounds like a fit, head to our website and book a call.
        </div></div> <div data-test-uiratingsummary="" data-test-partner-reviews="" class="flex gap-x-1"><div data-test-uirating="" class="flex items-center"><div data-test-star="0"><div data-test-uiratingstar="" class="pointer-events-none h-5 w-5"><div class="relative h-full w-full"><!----> <div class="absolute left-0 top-0 h-full overflow-hidden w-full"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" width="24px" height="24px" class="text-icon-award h-5 w-5"><path d="M9.049 2.927c.3-.921 1.603-.921 1.902 0l1.07 3.292a1 1 0 00.95.69h3.462c.969 0 1.371 1.24.588 1.81l-2.8 2.034a1 1 0 00-.364 1.118l1.07 3.292c.3.921-.755 1.688-1.54 1.118l-2.8-2.034a1 1 0 00-1.175 0l-2.8 2.034c-.784.57-1.838-.197-1.539-1.118l1.07-3.292a1 1 0 00-.364-1.118L2.98 8.72c-.783-.57-.38-1.81.588-1.81h3.461a1 1 0 00.951-.69l1.07-3.292z"></path></svg></div></div></div></div><div data-test-star="1"><div data-test-uiratingstar="" class="pointer-events-none h-5 w-5"><div class="relative h-full w-full"><!----> <div class="absolute left-0 top-0 h-full overflow-hidden w-full"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" width="24px" height="24px" class="text-icon-award h-5 w-5"><path d="M9.049 2.927c.3-.921 1.603-.921 1.902 0l1.07 3.292a1 1 0 00.95.69h3.462c.969 0 1.371 1.24.588 1.81l-2.8 2.034a1 1 0 00-.364 1.118l1.07 3.292c.3.921-.755 1.688-1.54 1.118l-2.8-2.034a1 1 0 00-1.175 0l-2.8 2.034c-.784.57-1.838-.197-1.539-1.118l1.07-3.292a1 1 0 00-.364-1.118L2.98 8.72c-.783-.57-.38-1.81.588-1.81h3.461a1 1 0 00.951-.69l1.07-3.292z"></path></svg></div></div></div></div><div data-test-star="2"><div data-test-uiratingstar="" class="pointer-events-none h-5 w-5"><div class="relative h-full w-full"><!----> <div class="absolute left-0 top-0 h-full overflow-hidden w-full"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" width="24px" height="24px" class="text-icon-award h-5 w-5"><path d="M9.049 2.927c.3-.921 1.603-.921 